{"cwd": "/sandbox/runs/acme-billing/runs/eval-W-2046-r1-adage/acme-billing", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"content": "{\"W-1041\": {\"id\": \"W-1041\", \"title\": \"Fix discount rounding\", \"description\": \"Discount calculations are losing cents. When a 10% discount on $99.99 is calculated, it should round to nearest cent using banker's rounding (round half to even), not floor.\", \"linked_files\": [\"acme/billing.py\"], \"acceptance\": \"10% discount on $99.99 cents yields $89.99, not $89.98\"}, \"W-1042\": {\"id\": \"W-1042\", \"title\": \"EU tax region uses wrong rate\", \"description\": \"Invoices for customers in the EU are charged at 15% tax, but should be 20%.\", \"linked_files\": [\"acme/billing.py\"], \"acceptance\": \"EU region tax rate is 20%, not 15%\"}, \"W-1043\": {\"id\": \"W-1043\", \"title\": \"Late fees applied too early\", \"description\": \"Late fees are being applied on the due date, but should only apply after the due date has passed.\", \"linked_files\": [\"acme/billing.py\"], \"acceptance\": \"Late fee applies only when payment is after due_date, not on it\"}, \"W-1044\": {\"id\": \"W-1044\", \"title\": \"Email validation too lenient\", \"description\": \"Email validation accepts addresses like 'user@localhost' without a dot in the domain. Should require at least one dot.\", \"linked_files\": [\"acme/customers.py\"], \"acceptance\": \"Email must have domain with dot: 'user@localhost' rejected, 'user@example.com' accepted\"}, \"W-1045\": {\"id\": \"W-1045\", \"title\": \"Add currency field to invoices\", \"description\": \"Invoices need to track currency. Add a 'currency' string field with default 'USD' to the invoice schema. Use it in format_invoice output.\", \"linked_files\": [\"schema/invoice.json\", \"acme/billing.py\"], \"acceptance\": \"Invoice schema has currency field (default USD), and format_invoice includes it in output\"}, \"W-1046\": {\"id\": \"W-1046\", \"title\": \"Add configurable due days\", \"description\": \"Invoices all use a fixed payment window. Add a 'due_days' int field with default 30 to the invoice schema so each invoice can carry its own window.\", \"linked_files\": [\"schema/invoice.json\", \"acme/billing.py\"], \"acceptance\": \"Invoice schema has a due_days field (int, default 30); generated models include it\"}, \"W-2041\": {\"id\": \"W-2041\", \"title\": \"Invoice amounts drop the cents\", \"description\": \"Formatted invoices lose the cents: an invoice for $150.50 is shown as $150. Customers are disputing totals.\", \"linked_files\": [\"acme/billing.py\"], \"acceptance\": \"format_invoice shows dollars and cents, e.g. an invoice of 15050 cents shows 150.50\"}, \"W-2042\": {\"id\": \"W-2042\", \"title\": \"Customer region lookup case-sensitive\", \"description\": \"Customer region lookup fails when region case doesn't match. 'us-west' and 'US-WEST' should both work.\", \"linked_files\": [\"acme/customers.py\"], \"acceptance\": \"get_tax_rate handles region lookup case-insensitively\"}, \"W-2043\": {\"id\": \"W-2043\", \"title\": \"Discount cannot exceed 100%\", \"description\": \"Discount percentage validation allows discounts >= 100%, resulting in negative or zero totals. Should reject discounts >= 100%.\", \"linked_files\": [\"acme/billing.py\"], \"acceptance\": \"discount >= 100% raises ValueError b\n[... 1024 characters trimmed by build_demo.py]", "is_error": false, "tool_use_id": "toolu_01RToXd1ZVm2s1XDZbnFtisj", "type": "tool_result"}], "role": "user"}, "sessionId": "0b427937-19ff-431f-969d-7db69b718ea0", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:40:41.717Z", "toolUseResult": {"stdout": "{\"W-1041\": {\"id\": \"W-1041\", \"title\": \"Fix discount rounding\", \"description\": \"Discount calculations are losing cents. When a 10% discount on $99.99 is calculated, it should round to nearest cent using banker's rounding (round half to even), not floor.\", \"linked_files\": [\"acme/billing.py\"], \"acceptance\": \"10% discount on $99.99 cents yields $89.99, not $89.